## Two things your merge-tree analysis couldn't see, and why

**1. A third conflict, `rescale_test.go`, surfaced mid-replay (commit 20/27) that your 2-file blast-
radius table doesn't list.** Not a bug in your analysis — `git merge-tree` computes one 3-way merge of
the *final* diff; an incremental `--onto` replay does N sequential 3-way merges, and an intermediate
step can collide even when the final states wouldn't. Shape: main added a
`Describe("rescaleModelDecisions", ...)` block immediately before where our own `Describe("fillRole",
...)` was inserted — "both independently added at the same point," not a divergent edit. Resolved by
keeping both, main's first.

**2. Two files auto-merged with *no* conflict markers but still broke** — `go vet` and a golden
assertion caught it, git's line-level merge could not. Main added tests calling `resolveITLModel`,
`computeVariantSupply`, and `validITLModel` with their pre-C10 signatures (missing the `kSat` parameter
C10 added) in regions our own commits never touched, so git saw no textual collision. Fixed by
threading `fallbackKSat` through each call site, matching the already-correct sibling test next to
each one. Committed separately as `8c335893` rather than folded into any rebased commit — it's a post-
rebase fixup, not part of any commit's original intent, and folding it in would mean rewriting history
nobody asked me to touch.

